      "rationale": "🩹️ RECLASSIFIED (ticket SEPARATE-ARTIFACT-STANDARD-SUBSET-IMPLEMENTATIONS-AND-FIXTURE-TEST-EVERY-MUTATION, shard A10, 2026-09-02). This entry was registered `third-party-library` on the strength of a real crate that does genuine codec work, but the mutation's expected RESULT is computed by this owner's own `🦀️oracle.rs` -- its dispatch function's catch-all arm is `\"mutation kind {...} has no oracle implementation\"`, proof that every OTHER arm is an implementation, not a reading. Both halves of the comparison then descend from the same specification, so a shared misreading produces two agreeing wrong answers -- the one failure a differential oracle exists to catch. This is a `cross-semio-implementation`: a required SUPPLEMENT (metamorphic/inverse/round-trip evidence), never a substitute. A qualifying third-party reference for the mutation semantics is still owed. See $TICKET/📓️a10-oracle-honesty.md.\n\nquick-xml is a general streaming XML reader AND writer, not an SVG library and not a profile validator. This subset's oracle (../🦀️oracle.rs) builds its own element tree from quick-xml's event stream through the shared 📰markup family module, resolves clip-path url(#id) references and applies the profile's clip-to-text and excluded-raster-primitive rules from its own transcription of REC-SVGMobile-20030114, and re-serializes with quick-xml's Writer. It never imports this repository's own SVG codec or its check_svg_basic_conformance.",
